<testgrp id="RM0000006XI02BX_01_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AD700000">
<testtitle>Service Inspection (AVC-LAN Connection Check)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Service Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E146276J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<table>
<title>Service Inspection Screen Display Contents</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.50in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.63in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Display</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Meaning</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Device Name</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Displays names, including retrofitted parts (displays the physical address if the name is unknown)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Inspection Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Displays the inspection result</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When diagnosis starts, the "Service Inspection" screen is displayed and the service inspection is performed.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The service inspection displays the inspection results on the screen based on information such as each component's response to the "system inspection command" and "diagnosis memory presentation request" and the "normal diagnosis notification".</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The screen is an example; depending on the connected devices, such as dealer-installed options, the device names displayed may differ from the actual screen.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The names of connected devices are displayed from the upper left in ascending order of physical address.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<test2>
<ptxt>Check that all of the following connected devices are displayed.</ptxt>
